                            <comment id="498603" author="arshad512" created="Mon, 27 Jul 2026 11:09:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;+1 On master: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/15fc6bd9-4fd2-401e-bb94-c1b1b35de28b&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/15fc6bd9-4fd2-401e-bb94-c1b1b35de28b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="503179" author="JIRAUSER24100" created="Sat, 10 Oct 2026 15:33:54 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Duplicate of &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20896&quot; title=&quot;O_DIRECT write &amp;gt;1MiB of encrypted file with key loaded corrupts data&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20896&quot;&gt;LU-20896&lt;/a&gt;. sanity-sec test_52 fails because an O_DIRECT write to an encrypted file, from a buffer page at a non-zero offset inside a transparent huge page, is encrypted with the wrong block index, so mirror verify then sees corrupt data. &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/69505&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69505&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20896&quot; title=&quot;O_DIRECT write &amp;gt;1MiB of encrypted file with key loaded corrupts data&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20896&quot;&gt;LU-20896&lt;/a&gt; osc: encrypt direct IO pages at their own file index) fixes it: on rocky10, a test_52 loop failed 4 times in 1500 iterations without the patch and 0 times in 4500 with it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
